59
00:05:06,221 --> 00:05:09,060
south to 26th Street.

60
00:05:09,061 --> 00:05:14,000
And on the east side, the Long Island Railroad will get eight new tracks, bringing riders

61
00:05:14,001 --> 00:05:16,540
to Grand Central Terminal.

62
00:05:16,541 --> 00:05:20,980
With the stakes higher than ever in the battle to keep New York's subway dry, the city is

63
00:05:20,981 --> 00:05:25,140
turning to this waterproof membrane to prevent leakage in the new tunnels.

64
00:05:25,141 --> 00:05:30,740
The tunnel membrane is made of PVC. You might know it is vinyl. This is very

65
00:05:30,741 --> 00:05:35,140
similar to the material that would be used in shower curtains, except that it's

66
00:05:35,141 --> 00:05:39,460
about 10 times as thick as a shower curtain, but with the same flexibility

67
00:05:39,461 --> 00:05:45,160
and waterproof qualities. Waterproofing is really all about molecular stickiness.

68
00:05:45,161 --> 00:05:50,040
This is a water molecule. You have two hydrogen's and an oxygen. This side of

69
00:05:50,041 --> 00:05:55,020
molecule is relatively positive and this side is relatively negative. Think of it

70
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:59,760
like the poles of a magnet. It wants to adhere to itself but as you can see it

71
00:05:59,761 --> 00:06:04,560
can also want to adhere to surfaces. So waterproofing is like putting a barrier

72
00:06:04,561 --> 00:06:10,600
between the water molecules and the surface such that they would prefer to

73
00:06:10,601 --> 00:06:16,480
stick to one another. The PVC membrane is a water barrier that can stretch unlike

74
00:06:16,481 --> 00:06:20,800
stiffer high-density plastics used in some other systems.

75
00:06:20,801 --> 00:06:26,240
Here, that flexibility is expanded by installing the membrane without ever puncturing it.

76
00:06:26,241 --> 00:06:31,540
To begin, workers secure a layer of either felt or geotextile with nails, as another

77
00:06:31,541 --> 00:06:32,540
technology.

78
00:06:32,541 --> 00:06:37,480
This layer helps drain water and provides protection for the waterproof membrane.

79
00:06:37,481 --> 00:06:43,980
Then, the crew nails down the felt with its attached PVC discs.

80
00:06:43,981 --> 00:06:48,440
The yellow membrane is then heat sealed to the PVC discs, instead of nailing it to the

81
00:06:48,441 --> 00:06:50,940
wall.

82
00:06:50,941 --> 00:06:55,380
In other systems, the membrane is directly attached to the wall with nails, so it may

83
00:06:55,381 --> 00:06:59,360
tear or leak when the rock shifts.

84
00:06:59,361 --> 00:07:06,100
By welding the membrane to PVC discs, the system has more flexibility and is watertight.

85
00:07:06,101 --> 00:07:12,740
You shouldn't penetrate the actual waterproofing membrane, but that's the reason we developed

86
00:07:12,741 --> 00:07:17,280
these disks so that there's no hole made in the membrane, nothing.

87
00:07:17,281 --> 00:07:22,320
No matter the level of precaution, leaks in the subway are always possible.

88
00:07:22,321 --> 00:07:26,020
In older systems, it's hard to plug the source because water can travel the whole length

89
00:07:26,021 --> 00:07:27,020
of the tunnel.

90
00:07:27,021 --> 00:07:30,460
You really go in and pump grouse to keep the water out.

91
00:07:30,461 --> 00:07:32,740
The problem with that is that it's a labor-intensive thing.

92
00:07:32,741 --> 00:07:36,660
You have to come over and over to do that.

93
00:07:36,661 --> 00:07:38,300
Water seeks the path of least resistance.

94
00:07:38,301 --> 00:07:42,580
If it's blocked in one part of the tunnel, it'll travel as far as it needs to go until

95
00:07:42,581 --> 00:07:45,760
it finds the next crack.

96
00:07:45,761 --> 00:07:52,460
You push the water further, further, further, further, so it can be that you have to route

97
00:07:52,461 --> 00:07:54,780
the complete tunnel.

98
00:07:54,781 --> 00:08:01,660
To make repairs easier, the crew installs ribbed vinyl barriers every 50 feet.

99
00:08:01,661 --> 00:08:06,080
These divide the tunnel up into individual sections, allowing for more targeted repairs

100
00:08:06,081 --> 00:08:08,080
from water damage.

101
00:08:08,081 --> 00:08:14,760
We know exactly the leak can only be between these two water barriers.

102
00:08:14,761 --> 00:08:21,340
Once the membrane is up, the crew erects a steel rebar grid that they welded together.

103
00:08:21,341 --> 00:08:25,400
This will serve as the reinforcement for the final concrete structure that will complete

104
00:08:25,401 --> 00:08:27,960
the tunnel.

105
00:08:27,961 --> 00:08:34,180
According to Wisco, this state-of-the-art system has a 100% success rate.

106
00:08:34,181 --> 00:08:38,940
New Yorkers are surrounded on all sides by water, but they're pushing back with everything

107
00:08:38,941 --> 00:08:41,140
they've got.

108
00:08:41,141 --> 00:08:46,600
The MTA is counting on new and better waterproofing technology to keep more than 1.5 billion riders

109
00:08:46,601 --> 00:08:50,420
yearly moving efficiently through the city.

110
00:08:50,421 --> 00:08:55,900
Bottom line is that the better the waterproofing, the better the subway will be.

111
00:08:55,901 --> 00:08:59,780
New York without the subway will be another village.

112
00:08:59,781 --> 00:09:02,300
We now return to waterproof on Modern Marvels.

113
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:10,620
The modern submarine is a sleek, powerful vessel that defies the many tons of water pressing in around it.

