00:14:09,221 --> 00:14:13,460
The damaging power of water is unquestionable.

187
00:14:13,461 --> 00:14:19,120
In a flash, rain can ruin millions of dollars of equipment for the military, firefighters,

188
00:14:19,121 --> 00:14:22,080
and first responders.

189
00:14:22,081 --> 00:14:30,000
In harsh and sometimes wet conditions, watertight cases are essential to protect equipment.

190
00:14:30,001 --> 00:14:36,260
Pelican cases were invented in the 1970s in the garage of a man named Dave Parker.

191
00:14:36,261 --> 00:14:40,860
Parker was a diver who wanted rugged equipment he could use in and around the water, so he

192
00:14:40,861 --> 00:14:42,791
started making it himself.

193
00:14:42,792 --> 00:14:48,360
Today at its headquarters in Torrance, California, Pelican makes watertight

194
00:14:48,361 --> 00:14:50,016
lights and dive gear.

195
00:14:50,017 --> 00:14:55,300
But it's best known for its nearly indestructible watertight cases,

196
00:14:55,301 --> 00:14:57,800
all ready to take on harsh conditions.

197
00:14:57,801 --> 00:15:04,180
It could be a hurricane, it could be dropped out of the back of vehicles, things like that.

198
00:15:04,181 --> 00:15:09,920
So the whole case is constructed to be robust in those environments.

199
00:15:09,921 --> 00:15:15,020
The glass vase goes in and the case goes over.

200
00:15:15,021 --> 00:15:21,680
Pelican prides itself on the toughness of its product testing.

201
00:15:21,681 --> 00:15:28,160
Throughout manufacturing, workers run through patented steps to make the cases watertight

202
00:15:28,161 --> 00:15:32,620
with the help of their mechanical colleagues.

203
00:15:32,621 --> 00:15:37,920
Domingo Acevedo has worked at Pelican for 10 years and supervises production on the floor.

204
00:15:37,921 --> 00:15:40,920
This is Shamu, this is an 1100 ton machine.

205
00:15:40,921 --> 00:15:46,920
And what you see right now coming out, being assembled over on this side, is the 1520 case.

206
00:15:46,921 --> 00:15:51,920
The cases are made of a plastic resin that's stored in silos as pellets.

207
00:15:51,921 --> 00:15:54,920
They're piped into hoppers where they're mixed with various colors.

208
00:15:54,921 --> 00:15:58,920
The pellets are then sent to production stations around the factory,

209
00:15:58,921 --> 00:16:02,920
where they're cooked at very high heat and injected into a mold or tool.

210
00:16:02,921 --> 00:16:06,920
This is a long barrel and that barrel is running at about 420 degrees.

211
00:16:06,921 --> 00:16:13,360
It melts the material, it pushes the material inside the tool, and then it has a cooling period.

212
00:16:13,361 --> 00:16:19,680
Once it cools enough, the robot will come pick it up, drop it down on the line, and then everything gets assembled from there.

213
00:16:19,681 --> 00:16:30,800
Now the workers take over to put on latches and the crucial O-ring, a neoprene band that seals the edge of the case, just like an O-ring seals a submarine edge.

214
00:16:30,801 --> 00:16:35,180
This makes it watertight.

215
00:16:35,181 --> 00:16:39,760
Not only the O-ring, but also the latches are very, very important because that's what

216
00:16:39,761 --> 00:16:44,760
gives it the tension and the pressure to keep that O-ring in place to make sure that it's

217
00:16:44,761 --> 00:16:45,760
watertight.

218
00:16:45,761 --> 00:16:49,700
We don't want to make it to where it's impossible to open, but we also want to make it to where

219
00:16:49,701 --> 00:16:52,700
if it drops, it doesn't pop open by itself.

220
00:16:52,701 --> 00:16:57,040
To make their cases even more watertight, Pelican uses a latch without springs.

221
00:16:57,041 --> 00:17:01,040
All there is is just a pin that holds the lever and the latch in place.

222
00:17:01,041 --> 00:17:05,040
You can put it in anything, it'll never rust, it'll never get stuck.

223
00:17:05,041 --> 00:17:07,040
And that's the reason why we don't use any springs on this.

224
00:17:07,041 --> 00:17:12,040
And Pelican also uses a purge valve, which keeps the pressure inside the case equalized.

225
00:17:12,041 --> 00:17:17,040
It'll let the air go out, but it never allows the water or anything to go inside.

