00:34:23,101 --> 00:34:27,760
This is another way to channel water away from the house.

456
00:34:27,761 --> 00:34:30,720
The boards ensure that any water that gets near the wall

457
00:34:30,721 --> 00:34:34,900
will be directed down to what's called a French drain.

458
00:34:34,901 --> 00:34:37,740
This has holes in it, holes face down.

459
00:34:37,741 --> 00:34:40,300
We're giving the water a path of least resistance to run.

460
00:34:40,301 --> 00:34:41,340
We have gravel underneath.

461
00:34:41,341 --> 00:34:42,780
We cover this with gravel on top.

462
00:34:44,380 --> 00:34:46,980
And that way, any water that runs along our vapor barriers,

463
00:34:47,140 --> 00:34:48,880
everything that we've done from the top of the roof

464
00:34:48,881 --> 00:34:50,260
all the way down to the foundation

465
00:34:50,261 --> 00:34:52,960
is going to find the path of loose resistance, which is this pipe.

466
00:34:54,480 --> 00:34:55,900
And this all drains into a sump pump,

467
00:34:55,980 --> 00:34:57,460
which gets pumped out into our storm drains.

468
00:34:58,480 --> 00:35:02,920
Advances in waterproofing homes give us new weapons in the battle for dryness.

469
00:35:03,900 --> 00:35:06,820
Next, an invention for cars that locks water out.

470
00:35:07,140 --> 00:35:09,780
And your iPod gets wet? Relax.

471
00:35:09,781 --> 00:35:12,780
Next, on Modern Marvels.

472
00:35:12,781 --> 00:35:18,780
We now return to Waterproof on Modern Marvels.

473
00:35:18,781 --> 00:35:21,780
Water is a part of us.

474
00:35:21,781 --> 00:35:23,780
60% to be exact.

475
00:35:23,781 --> 00:35:26,780
Yet we too are ingeniously waterproof.

476
00:35:26,781 --> 00:35:31,780
Our skin repels water, but lets moisture escape from inside.

477
00:35:31,781 --> 00:35:35,780
Humans and animals have natural waterproofing with your skin.

478
00:35:35,781 --> 00:35:40,340
If you didn't, going swimming or going out in the rain would be a very dangerous proposition.

479
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:46,280
Plants and animals have similar strategies for controlling evaporation and hydration.

480
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:50,240
Many birds have a special gland that produces oil.

481
00:35:51,100 --> 00:35:53,380
The oil keeps their feathers waterproof and buoyant.

482
00:35:54,480 --> 00:35:57,060
Sea otters keep warm and dry with two layers of fur.

483
00:35:57,580 --> 00:36:01,700
The outer hairs are long and waterproof, protecting a thicker, shorter layer underneath.

484
00:36:01,701 --> 00:36:09,060
In an arid region of Argentina, the Argentinian monkey frog secretes wax from specialized

485
00:36:09,061 --> 00:36:14,000
glands in its skin to form a barrier against water loss.

486
00:36:14,001 --> 00:36:20,240
The frogs are waterproofing their skin with their own blend of wax.

487
00:36:20,241 --> 00:36:23,620
Waxes are a combination of fatty acids and alcohols.

488
00:36:23,621 --> 00:36:28,280
They usually melt at temperatures above 113 degrees Fahrenheit.

489
00:36:28,281 --> 00:36:35,120
they're insoluble, waxes provide us yet another way to waterproof.

490
00:36:35,121 --> 00:36:39,680
It wasn't long after Henry Ford figured out how to mass produce the automobile, that people

491
00:36:39,681 --> 00:36:43,480
began applying wax to their cars.

492
00:36:43,481 --> 00:36:49,460
Simon Eyes, named after its founder, George Simons, began mass producing car wax in 1911.

493
00:36:49,461 --> 00:36:56,680
You can now find Simon Eyes in the dictionary, defined as to shine or polish to a high sheen,

494
00:36:56,681 --> 00:36:58,440
especially with wax.

495
00:36:58,441 --> 00:37:02,180
Simonize wax protection against road chemicals, fumes, rust.

496
00:37:02,181 --> 00:37:06,000
The company promoted the idea of shiny cars and glamour.

497
00:37:06,001 --> 00:37:08,300
Give your car Simonize wax protection.

498
00:37:08,301 --> 00:37:10,960
Sorry, old girl, wrong button.

499
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:14,760
But there's a science behind it, and

500
00:37:14,761 --> 00:37:17,840
it has to do with the way wax molecules behave.

501
00:37:17,841 --> 00:37:21,280
One end of the molecule adheres to the paint.

502
00:37:21,281 --> 00:37:25,500
The other end that now is shown to the world is something that the water doesn't

503
00:37:25,501 --> 00:37:29,520
want to stick to. This is how you know you have good wax jobs when the water

504
00:37:29,521 --> 00:37:34,500
beads up on it. Wax is wonderfully water repellent but it doesn't stay on cars

505
00:37:34,501 --> 00:37:39,260
for more than a few months. For car owners the holy grail has been a coating

506
00:37:39,261 --> 00:37:44,460
that would permanently protect their car from all kinds of harsh elements. Here at

507
00:37:44,461 --> 00:37:48,360
headquarters in Bolton, Connecticut the Simonized company believes they found a

508
00:37:48,361 --> 00:37:54,120
unique waterproofing product. Glass coat because it doesn't need to be reapplied

509
00:37:54,121 --> 00:37:57,603
applied every few months. They call it the anti-wax.

510
00:37:57,604 --> 00:37:59,880
Chemist David White invented glass

511
00:37:59,881 --> 00:38:04,000
coat after conducting endless experiments on his own car.

512
00:38:04,001 --> 00:38:11,280
I probably went through five or six hundred formulations and I just kept grinding away

513
00:38:11,281 --> 00:38:17,060
at it, zeroing in on the precise application and then it didn't do anything that it shouldn't

514
00:38:17,061 --> 00:38:21,240
have done. It did everything it should have done and I said, aha.

515
00:38:21,241 --> 00:38:27,740
Simonize closely guards their secret, but the key ingredient is a chemical compound called polysilosane.

516
00:38:28,380 --> 00:38:35,700
Its waterproof properties make it an effective coating for bridges, solar panels, and tiles on NASA's space shuttles.

517
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:42,020
Glass Coat takes the useful properties of polysilosane into the world of cars.

518
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:47,980
Polysilosane reacts with hydrogen and oxygen, and it forms microns of glass on top of the clear coat.

519
00:38:47,981 --> 00:38:56,258
And those microns of glass are what help keep this product very hydrophobic and also protects it for a long period of time against tree sap, bird waste, insects,

520
00:38:56,259 --> 00:38:58,160
anything that can eat the clear coat.

521
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:02,900
Polysilazane is a compound made of silicon nitrogen molecules.

522
00:39:04,040 --> 00:39:08,580
The nitrogen reacts with water vapor to catalyze a bond between silicon and oxygen.

523
00:39:09,380 --> 00:39:16,860
When the silicon and oxygen come together, they form a super hard glass, which acts as an effective barrier to the many enemies of car surfaces.

524
00:39:16,861 --> 00:39:19,600
from a car wash to acid rain.

525
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:23,340
Acid rain is formed by particulates up in the air

526
00:39:23,341 --> 00:39:25,420
that are typically sulfur dioxide.

527
00:39:25,840 --> 00:39:27,540
The water falls down to the hard surface,

528
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:29,080
in this case the paint of a vehicle,

529
00:39:29,340 --> 00:39:32,340
and when it evaporates, the perimeter of the water drop

530
00:39:32,341 --> 00:39:35,680
heats up and it puts an acid etch on the car.

531
00:39:36,460 --> 00:39:38,000
With the application of glass coat,

532
00:39:38,580 --> 00:39:41,280
Simon Eyes guarantees protection of a vehicle's top coat

533
00:39:41,281 --> 00:39:42,440
for seven years.

534
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:45,660
So you've got the base metal, you have a primer,

535
00:39:45,661 --> 00:39:48,340
you have the color paint, you have the clear coat on top of that.

536
00:39:48,820 --> 00:39:51,840
Glass Coat goes on top of that and protects the entire system underneath.

537
00:39:52,760 --> 00:39:57,440
Glass Coat's waterproof properties have been tested by Simon Eyes and university researchers.

538
00:39:58,200 --> 00:40:00,680
After applying Glass Coat to only one side of the hood,

539
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:04,460
they ran the car through an industrial wash a hundred times.

540
00:40:08,220 --> 00:40:10,980
The half without the protection was wet after the wash,

541
00:40:11,340 --> 00:40:14,380
but the other side sheaths or sheds the water

542
00:40:14,381 --> 00:40:16,820
so that it beads up and rolls off.

543
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:20,980
A practical application of cutting-edge waterproofing science.

544
00:40:23,540 --> 00:40:27,300
These days, waterproofing isn't just for mountain climbers or firefighters.

545
00:40:27,940 --> 00:40:29,320
Now it can go poolside.

546
00:40:30,960 --> 00:40:35,000
Objects that used to be completely destroyed by water are now water-friendly.

547
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:42,860
We may have a love-hate relationship with water,

548
00:40:42,861 --> 00:40:49,860
But advances in waterproofing materials and technology are giving us a greater ability to work, live, and play in it.

549
00:40:49,861 --> 00:40:53,860
Now, we can go singing in the rain.

